From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mihawk <163614687+mihawk-99@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: PS5: memory asked to be exported is ordinary memory when there is no host handle type

Every game's Vulkan on the console is the GPU broker's client, which offers no
external memory, so get_host_external_memory_type() is 0. An allocation with a
VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo then got no host handle, no D3DKMT resource, and
failed with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY: a Direct3D 12 game that makes a shared
resource at start (Unreal Engine 5) closed. With no host handle type the export
request is now dropped and the memory is ordinary; vkGetMemoryWin32HandleKHR on
memory that was neither exported nor imported returns
VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE with no handle, where it reported success.
VKD3D-Proton stops asking for the export without the extension
(platform/vkd3d-proton/patches/0003); this keeps any other client's request
from failing the allocation.

The problem was found by reading prospero-win 0054 as PC5 carries it
(github.com/bornaradusin/PC5 at 81323dc3, LGPL-2.1); this patch is
independently written.
---
--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -1618,6 +1618,14 @@
             export_info = (VkExportMemoryAllocateInfo *)*next;
             if (!(export_info->handleTypes & EXTERNAL_MEMORY_WIN32_BITS))
                 FIXME( "Unsupported handle types %#x\n", export_info->handleTypes );
+            else if (!get_host_external_memory_type())
+            {
+                /* No host type to export through (the PS5's GPU broker client): the export used to fail the whole
+                 * allocation, so the memory is an ordinary allocation, and a handle asked of it later is refused. */
+                WARN( "No host external memory type: allocating without export\n" );
+                export_info = NULL;
+                *next = (*next)->pNext; next = &prev;
+            }
             else
             {
                 nt_shared = !(export_info->handleTypes & (VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_OPAQUE_WIN32_KMT_BIT |
@@ -1802,6 +1810,14 @@
 
     TRACE( "device %p, handle_info %p, handle %p\n", device, handle_info, handle );
 
+    if (!memory->local)
+    {
+        /* Neither exported nor imported (an export with no host type, vkAllocateMemory): there is no handle. */
+        WARN( "Memory %p has no shared resource\n", memory );
+        *handle = NULL;
+        return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+    }
+
     switch (handle_info->handleType)
     {
     case VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_OPAQUE_WIN32_KMT_BIT:
